 already prices), and the drop's last step not braked to the set point on a rhythm concept.
 
 Guard, scan, provenance and dither pass.
+
+### B, second mechanism (Integration's ruling), built and re-diagnosed
+
+On a concept with a rhythm throw (quick game, or read 1 on time at the set in the plan), his last drop step is not
+braked (RHYTHM_PLANT 0.4 of top speed, chosen), and at the plant he throws read 1 on anticipation if ready() (his forecast
+of the break against a throw started now) and it clears his bar; else he sets and hitches.
+Games (8, seed 11), QB_DRIVE / + QB_RHYTHM_THROW / + THROW_PLATFORM: no-set 4 / 4 / 5%; rhythm throws 0 / 2 / 2 of
+~700; catch 0.683 / 0.699 / 0.696; ints 8 / 4 / 14; pbu 62 / 89 / 58. Quick game snap to release 2.25 / 2.15 / 2.15 s.
+Staged 1536 (DRIVE / +RHYTHM): sacks 3.4 / 3.0%, completions 946 / 935, ints 10 / 13, yd 7.52 / 7.03.
+Why it still fires on 2 throws (scripts: a plant-time gate probe, 8 concepts x 16 plays): the quick concepts with a key
+(slant_flat, quick_outs, curl_flat, double_slants: 16 of 16 keyed) have not read the key by the plant, so read 1 is not
+yet named; on the unkeyed ones (stick, hitches) read 1 is ready-by-release (5 / 16, 16 / 16) but priced under his bar
+(7 / 16 each over it): the break comes 0.17-0.55 s after the release, and the window prices a man who has not broken as
+covered. Two attempts at this mechanism; not tweaked a third time. The next pieces are the key cued on the plant on a
+quick concept, and how the window prices an anticipation throw before the break (a question of the price, shared with
+the open-receiver underrating).
